WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:03.540
Speaker 1: OK, let's follow up on a couple
of different stories that we've been covering

00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:10.360
for some time, you might remember that sort
of in the in the middle of the 2020 era of

00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:15.550
the pandemic, there was this plot to kidnap
the Democratic Michigan governor, Gretchen

00:00:15.550 --> 00:00:18.080
Whitmer, and a number of people were arrested
for that.

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:24.070
We have now learned what the consequences
will be for one of the coconspirators, I guess

00:00:24.070 --> 00:00:25.100
we would call them there.

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:30.250
A Michigan man who admitted to taking part
in an extremist groups plot to kidnap Gretchen

00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:36.140
Whitmer in retaliation for covid restrictions
was sentenced yesterday to over six years

00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:37.329
in prison.

00:00:37.329 --> 00:00:42.480
The man is 25 year old Tai Garbin is the only
person to have pleaded guilty out of the more

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:46.120
than a dozen men facing state and federal
charges stemming from the plot.

00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:50.530
So understand that this guy got more than
six years.

00:00:50.530 --> 00:00:52.760
He pleaded guilty and cooperated.

00:00:52.760 --> 00:00:58.469
The others are presumably going to trial and
this guy still got six years.

00:00:58.469 --> 00:01:03.510
So just think about what might be coming for
some of the other individuals here.

00:01:03.510 --> 00:01:09.490
Five of those charged in federal court pleaded
not guilty and face trial in October.

00:01:09.490 --> 00:01:16.119
U.S. District Judge Robert Jonker sentenced
Garbin to 75 months in prison, three years

00:01:16.119 --> 00:01:19.920
of probation and a 2500 dollar fine.

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:24.729
During the sentencing hearing, Garbin apologized
to Wittmer, who was not present.

00:01:24.729 --> 00:01:29.599
This guy essentially threw himself at the
mercy of the court, pleaded guilty, cooperated

00:01:29.599 --> 00:01:34.219
and apologized and still got more than six
years, at least in theory.

00:01:34.219 --> 00:01:39.240
Of course, it'll depend on exactly what charges
others are convicted of, if at all.

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:43.539
You could be looking at way longer prison
sentences for the others.

00:01:43.539 --> 00:01:48.399
The individual, Ty Garbin said, quote, First,
I would like to take this opportunity to apologize

00:01:48.399 --> 00:01:51.229
